# 必考词 Unit04
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit04核心高频词汇

{{channel}}{/ˈtʃænl/}{{n. 频道；渠道；海峡}}{{The company uses multiple channels to reach customers.}}

{{chapter}}{/ˈtʃæptər/}{{n. 章；回}}{{The first chapter introduces the main characters.}}

{{character}}{/ˈkærəktər/}{{n. 性格；角色；字符}}{{Honesty is an important character trait.}}

{{charge}}{/tʃɑːrdʒ/}{{v. 收费；指控；充电}}{{The hotel charges $200 per night for a double room.}}

{{charity}}{/ˈtʃærəti/}{{n. 慈善；慈善机构}}{{She donated a large sum of money to charity.}}

{{chemical}}{/ˈkemɪkl/}{{adj. 化学的；n. 化学品}}{{The factory produces various chemical products.}}

{{circulate}}{/ˈsɜːrkjəleɪt/}{{v. 循环；流通}}{{Blood circulates through the body continuously.}}

{{circumstance}}{/ˈsɜːrkəmstæns/}}{n. 环境；情况}}{{Under no circumstances should you reveal the password.}}

{{civil}}{/ˈsɪvl/}{{adj. 公民的；文明的}}{{Civil rights are protected by the constitution.}}

{{claim}}{/kleɪm/}}{v. 声称；索取}}{{He claimed that he was innocent of the crime.}}

{{clarify}}{/ˈklærɪfaɪ/}{{v. 澄清；阐明}}{{The teacher clarified the confusing concept for the students.}}

{{classify}}{/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/}}{v. 分类；归类}}{{The books are classified by subject in the library.}}

{{climate}}{/ˈklaɪmət/}{{n. 气候；风气}}{{Global warming is changing the climate patterns worldwide.}}

{{cling}}{/klɪŋ/}{{v. 紧贴；坚持}}{{The child clung to her mother's hand tightly.}}

{{coincide}}{/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd/}}{v. 同时发生；一致}}{{The two events coincided by pure coincidence.}}

{{collapse}}{/kəˈlæps/}}{v./n. 崩塌；垮台}}{{The old building collapsed during the earthquake.}}

{{colleague}}{/ˈkɒliːɡ/}}{n. 同事}}{{She gets along well with her colleagues at work.}}

{{combine}}{/kəmˈbaɪn/}}{v. 结合；联合}}{{The project combines theory with practical experience.}}

{{command}}{/kəˈmɑːnd/}}{v./n. 命令；掌握}}{{The officer commanded his soldiers to advance.}}

{{comment}}{/ˈkɒment/}}{n./v. 评论；意见}}{{The professor made several comments on the student's essay.}}

{{commission}}{/kəˈmɪʃn/}}{n. 委员会；佣金}}{{The government set up a commission to investigate the issue.}}

{{commit}}{/kəˈmɪt/}}{v. 犯（罪）；承诺；投入}}{{He committed himself to finishing the project on time.}}

{{committee}}{/kəˈmɪti/}{{n. 委员会}}{{The committee will review all the proposals next week.}}

{{communicate}}{/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/}}{v. 交流；传达}}{{It is important to communicate effectively with your team.}}

{{community}}{/kəˈmjuːnəti/}}{n. 社区；群体}}{{The local community organized a clean-up event.}}

{{companion}}{/kəmˈpæniən/}}{n. 同伴；伙伴}}{{The dog has been a loyal companion to the old man.}}

{{compare}}{/kəmˈpeər/}}{v. 比较；对比}}{{We compared the prices of different brands before buying.}}

{{compatible}}{/kəmˈpætəbl/}}{adj. 兼容的；合得来的}}{{The software is compatible with most operating systems.}}

{{compel}}{/kəmˈpel/}}{v. 强迫；迫使}}{{The evidence compelled the jury to reach a guilty verdict.}}

{{compensate}}{/ˈkɒmpənseɪt/}}{v. 补偿；赔偿}}{{The company compensated the workers for their overtime.}}

{{compete}}{/kəmˈpiːt/}}{v. 竞争；比赛}}{{Several companies compete for the same market share.}}

{{complain}}{/kəmˈpleɪn/}}{v. 抱怨；投诉}}{{Customers complained about the poor service quality.}}

{{complex}}{/ˈkɒmpleks/}}{adj. 复杂的；n. 综合体}}{{The human brain is an incredibly complex organ.}}

{{component}}{/kəmˈpəʊnənt/}}{n. 组成部分；部件}}{{Each component of the machine must function properly.}}

{{compose}}{/kəmˈpəʊz/}}{v. 组成；创作}}{{Water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen.}}

{{comprehensive}}{/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv/}}{adj. 全面的；综合的}}{{The report provides a comprehensive analysis of the market.}}

{{comprise}}{/kəmˈpraɪz/}}{v. 包含；由...组成}}{{The committee comprises twelve members from different departments.}}

{{compromise}}{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/}}{n./v. 妥协；折中}}{{Both sides reached a compromise after long negotiations.}}

{{conceal}}{/kənˈsiːl/}}{v. 隐藏；隐瞒}}{{He tried to conceal his disappointment with a smile.}}

{{concentrate}}{/ˈkɒnsntreɪt/}}{v. 集中；专心}}{{She concentrated on her studies and ignored distractions.}}
